course: dictionary
lesson: 6420
title: Mute: one word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and context tells you which one is meant. «You're on mute!» says a friend on a video call. Here mute means the sound is turned off, so nobody can hear you. Ask: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
explain: The same word can mean something very different in another sentence. «She stayed mute when the teacher asked her name.» Mute means silent, not speaking. The clue is that she did not answer. «The trumpet has a mute, and it makes the notes softer.» Here mute is a small object on an instrument, and the clue is softer.
explain: Mute can also describe colours and sounds. «The muted greens of the forest were calm and soft.» Muted means soft and not bright. Think of it as turned down, the way a sound is turned down, and the meaning will often come to you.
fact: Mute can be a verb, an adjective or a noun, depending on the sentence.
fact: As a verb, mute means to turn a sound off: «Please mute your microphone.»
fact: As an adjective, mute means silent or not speaking: «She stayed mute.» Muted colours and sounds are soft or not bright.
fact: As a noun, a mute is a device on a musical instrument, like a trumpet, that makes its sound quieter or different.
fact: Long ago, mute was used for a person who cannot speak, but this is old-fashioned and can hurt; say «non-speaking» instead.
exercise: «You're on mute!» In this sentence, what does mute mean? | Very loud and cheerful | Lost in the rain | *Turned off, so nobody can hear | Stuck high up in a tree
exercise: «She stayed mute when the teacher asked her name.» What does mute mean here? | Cold and wet | Running fast | *Silent, not speaking | Very loud and cheerful
exercise: «The muted greens of the forest were calm.» What does muted describe? | *Soft and not bright | Fast and noisy | Bright and shiny | Hot and dry
test: «Muting someone means you stop hearing them; it does not tell them anything.» What does this sentence say muting does? | Tells them off loudly | Makes them famous | Sends them a message | *Stops you hearing them, without telling them
test: On a trumpet, what does a mute do? | Lights it up | *Makes its sound quieter or different | Makes it louder | Stops it from being played
exam: «Muting a chat at night can help.» In this sentence, what does muting mean? | Deleting the chat forever | *Turning off the sound and alerts from the chat | Joining the chat | Shouting at the chat
